# Building AI Infrastructure - Cursor Rules

## Repository Overview
This is a Hugo-based static site using the PaperMod theme. It hosts technical blog posts, books, courses, and data about AI infrastructure and programming. The site is deployed at https://nvbkdw.github.io/

## Content Structure

### Blog Post Format
All blog posts must follow this frontmatter structure:
```yaml
---
title: "Post Title Here"
date: YYYY-MM-DD
tags: ["tag1","tag2","tag3"]
author: "Ryan H."
description: "Brief description of the post"
summary: "Brief summary of the post"
cover:
    image: "post-image.png"
    alt: "Alt text for image"
    relative: true
---
```

### Content Organization
- Blog posts: `/content/blogs/`
- Books: `/content/books/`
- Courses: `/content/courses/`
- Data: `/content/data/`
- Papers: `/content/papers/`

## Writing Guidelines

### Math and LaTeX
- Use inline math with single dollar signs: `$x = y + z$`
- Use display math with double dollar signs: `$$\int_0^1 f(x) dx$$`
- Common math sets: `$\mathbb{R}$`, `$\mathbb{N}$`, `$\mathbb{S}$`
- The site has math rendering enabled (`math: true` in config)
- Use proper LaTeX commands for mathematical expressions

### Code Blocks
- Use fenced code blocks with language specification:
  ````markdown
  ```python
  def example():
      return True
  ```
  ````
- Code copy buttons are enabled in the theme
- Supported languages include Python, JavaScript, CUDA, C++, etc.

### Markdown Structure
- Use H2 (`##`) for main sections (H1 is reserved for the title)
- Use bullet points (`-`) for lists
- Keep descriptions and summaries concise
- Use relative paths for images in the same directory

### Tags
- Use lowercase for tags
- Use hyphens for multi-word tags (e.g., "deep-learning", "gpu-kernel")
- Keep tags specific and relevant to AI infrastructure topics
- Common tags: "deep learning", "gpu", "inference", "distributed-training", "llm"

## Technical Details

### Hugo Configuration
- Theme: PaperMod
- Default theme: light (theme toggle disabled)
- Code highlighting: autumn style
- Date format: "January 2006"
- Pagination: 20 items per page

### Build and Deployment
- Hugo static site generator
- Deployed to GitHub Pages
- Base URL: https://nvbkdw.github.io/

## File Naming Conventions
- Blog post files: Use kebab-case (e.g., `gpu-kernel-programming-101.md`)
- Image files: Match the blog post name (e.g., `gpu-kernel-programming-101.png`)
- Use descriptive, SEO-friendly names

## Content Guidelines
- Focus on AI infrastructure, machine learning systems, and programming
- Include practical examples and code snippets where relevant
- Explain complex concepts clearly with proper mathematical notation
- Use diagrams and images to illustrate concepts
- Keep technical accuracy as the top priority

## When Creating New Blog Posts
1. Create a new `.md` file in `/content/blogs/`
2. Include complete frontmatter with all required fields
3. Add a corresponding cover image if available
4. Use proper heading hierarchy (start with H2)
5. Include relevant tags for discoverability
6. Ensure proper LaTeX formatting for mathematical content
7. Test locally before committing

## Avoid
- Don't use H1 headings in content (reserved for page title)
- Don't forget the frontmatter
- Don't use absolute paths for local images (use relative paths)
- Don't mix inline and display math syntax incorrectly
- Don't commit without testing Hugo build locally

